WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.800
A lot of

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.235
stuff to talk about

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.737
with Congress and Ukraine.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.138
I first want to ask you

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:05.705
about what

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.440
we're seeing in Monterey

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.809
Park, California, in your home state.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.345
Of Texas when a lot of mass shootings.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.513
You've all the Sutherland

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.683
Springs, El Paso, Santa Fe, you voted

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.152
no on bipartisan gun legislation

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.253
last summer.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:22.722
That got a pretty big bipartisan vote.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.258
It was pretty incremental also.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.793
Would you support any

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.362
gun control measures in this Congress?

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.096
You know,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.632
I was a counterterrorism prosecutor.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.701
I was chairman of Homeland Security.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.135
You know,

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:37.137
Chicago has probably the

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.505
some of the strictest gun

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.607
laws in the nation, yet

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.708
the highest murder rate.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.143
So, you know,

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.244
the way I look at it is

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.845
we need the intelligence.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.280
We need information sharing.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.015
We need to connect the dots.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.283
Every one of these cases,

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.451
and I guarantee you can see it

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.652
in this one as well.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.387
The shooter had warning

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.822
signs along the way.

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.824
We just didn't respond or pick it up.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.460
So in my judgment,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.561
we can create a system.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.896
I introduced a bill

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:03.696
that we could take

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:05.799
public information on the Internet,

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:08.068
have an algorithm to stop the threat

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.669
before it happens.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.671
That is a smart approach

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.806
rather than, you know,

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:14.574
violating Second Amendment rights.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:15.408
And so,

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:17.777
look, I hope we can get that passed.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.746
We're seeing this movie

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:20.680
way too many times.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.181
Yeah, we are.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:23.283
And it's it's absolutely tragic.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.984
What about a red flag law?

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:25.819
Federal red flag?

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:26.586
Well, in a way,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.922
what I'm talking about are red flags.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.056
And every one of these.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.057
But, you know,

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.359
Chicago, Illinois, you know, red flag.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.561
I know what you keep.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.829
You keep bringing up Chicago,

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.297
which I understand.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.532
But the guns in Chicago

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.034
come in from other places

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.336
because there are a patchwork of laws

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.471
across the country.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.738
There's no federal law.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.406
Right.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.307
Again,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:47.907
we stopped

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.943
and I saw it when I chaired Homeland.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.578
So many terror attacks

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:52.378
because we

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.514
got the threat information in advance

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:55.949
and we stopped it.

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:57.951
We can use that same formula

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.785
here, domestic

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.820
We although it's a little different,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.054
you know,

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.723
the Constitution didn't apply overseas.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.625
But we can do that here

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.960
and stop these threats

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.294
before they happen.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.330
Let's talk about Russia

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.332
and Russia's war on Ukraine.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.567
Ukraine is still asking for more help,

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.401
as you well know.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.738
You had pretty strong words about Germany

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.639
because Germany

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.474
so far is saying no

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:24.077
to transferring its tanks to Ukraine.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.979
You called it a cowardly decision.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.281
What seems like we're at

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.517
a pretty key moment in this war.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.651
What do you think

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.719
the Biden administration

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.320
should do differently with regard

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.322
to this particular standoff?

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.090
Well, the NATO

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.625
secretary general Stoltenberg

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.860
called it a pivotal moment.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.962
I think that we cannot slow walk

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.831
the weapons in.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.232
And, you know, even The Wall Street

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.767
Journal had a great editorial

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.768
and they said,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.035
you know,

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.337
there's no moral or strategic case

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.772
for giving Ukraine

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.806
just enough weapons

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.309
to to bleed for months,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.444
but not for victory.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.647
I've been a proponent of let's

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:01.681
give them what they need,

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.083
because when we do, they win.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.653
The tanks are vitally important.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.688
Why Because we know

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.957
with the new General Putin put in place,

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.992
they're going to start a major offensive

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.196
on the eastern flank in the Donbas.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.231
And we know that's going to happen.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.200
The tanks can help stop that.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.468
Germany will not put one tank in.

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.671
Member Germany, Nord Stream two pipeline.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.673
They won't put one take in

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.608
until we give them reassurances.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.043
We're going to put our Abrams out.

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.945
If we did that publicly,

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:32.912
that would unleash

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.214
so many Ledford tanks,

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.915
because there are ten other nations

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.317
that are looking for Germany.

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.219
To sign off on the tanks

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.987
that they have given them.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.822
That would be a game changer in addition

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:46.259
to tactical missiles called attack guns.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.560
They can reach Crimea

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.962
to take out the Iranian drone.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:49.329
So, Mr.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:49.662
Chairman,

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.966
are you arguing here for the US sending

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.802
Abrams tanks to Ukraine?

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:56.970
100%.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.339
We don't have to send very many.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.940
All we have to do is send enough

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:01.674
to unleash

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.076
what Germany has

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.644
and what the ten other countries

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:05.712
in Naito have.

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.680
Naito has to share the burden.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.882
One good thing that came out of Rammstein

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.284
Summit was that NATO

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.119
countries are sharing the burden.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.254
It's in their backyard.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.855
It's in their best interest,

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:16.956
and there's no concern

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.725
that this could be an escalation

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.293
in the eyes of Russia.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.961
You know, they said that with Stingers.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.297
They said that would you have on high?

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:25.198
I mean, what

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:27.934
I think I think Mr.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.102
Putin is a provocative

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:29.669
one here

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:30.470
who's escalated

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.504
as he invaded

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:33.306
a sovereign territory

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:36.209
aggressively unprovoked Mr.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:36.976
Chairman,

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.078
a lot of members of your conference,

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.413
fellow Republicans,

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.914
they want to stop giving money

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.316
to Ukraine.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.884
Should Ukraine be worried

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.585
that the money

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.153
is going to stop coming from the U.S.?

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:48.154
No, no.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.856
I think there's enough support

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:51.324
on both sides of the aisle,

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.392
majority in

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.060
the Democratic Party,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.229
majority in the Republican.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.497
The national security chairman,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.132
like myself, support this.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.933
We have to educate our members.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.802
I don't think they quite understand

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.237
what is at stake

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:05.605
if Ukraine falls

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:06.272
Chairman Xi

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:08.241
and China is going to invade Taiwan.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:11.644
If Russia, China, Iran is putting drones

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:12.512
in Crimea

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.413
and North Korea,

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:16.683
that's putting artillery into Russia.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.485
They have to understand the case

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.220
and they talk about the border.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.289
Not mutually exclusive at all.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.291
We can do both. We're a great country.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.060
We can walk and chew gum at the

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.628
same time. Let's talk about

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:30.496
some things happening

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.230
on the home front,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.633
specifically the revelation

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:36.369
last night that the FBI found six

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:37.770
more classified documents

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:38.838
at President Biden's

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.574
private home in Delaware,

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.709
and that was after

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:44.010
a 13 hour search,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.878
one that he invited

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.980
to get to the bottom of it.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.082
What is your reaction

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.117
and do you feel satisfied

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.686
now that the FBI has

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:56.022
what it needs and has everything?

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:56.489
I don't know,

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.790
because every day it seems like

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.125
they're finding more documents.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:00.360
And so I think

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.127
what's significant

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:02.729
is a former federal prosecutor

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.197
that no longer

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:04.797
they are relying

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.632
on the attorneys to comply,

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.302
although it was consensual, the search.

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.269
But the fact is,

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.504
the FBI conducted

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.639
this search, not his attorneys,

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.408
that that really ratchets

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:16.676
the investigation up.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:17.210
But as you said,

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.078
they invited the FBI to do so.

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:19.712
They did.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.181
And I think that's true.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:22.815
I don't know.

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:23.549
The DNI,

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.651
director of National Intelligence, won't

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.387
I give Congress any information

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.187
about the documents

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.757
I hear pertains to foreign adversaries?

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:32.024
I don't know.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:32.759
The Chinese

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.460
gave a 30 million contribution

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.429
in to University of Pennsylvania.

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.130
At the same time,

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.232
the Biden Center's being stood up.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.967
And what is their connection

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:43.436
on sending a letter out tomorrow

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:45.004
to the State Department's security?

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.105
Blinken

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.274
asking for what communications,

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.675
what contacts were made?

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.210
What were these documents

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.779
that were Chinese officials

00:06:52.779 --> 00:06:54.514
at the Biden Center

00:06:54.514 --> 00:06:56.549
And the fact that they're in the garage

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.918
with a Corvette and then a home

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.721
where Hunter Biden is recovering

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:03.356
and he took a picture of his laptop

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.891
of important documents.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.326
I just think,

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.095
Dana, there are a lot of unanswered

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:10.296
questions here. Yeah.

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:11.898
Just just for the record,

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:13.166
University of Pennsylvania said

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:13.966
the Chinese money

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.835
did not go to the Biden Center.

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.470
And we don't have any

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.838
evidence about Hunter Biden

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:19.772
being related to this.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.774
But they have a thousand talents program.

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:23.409
That's the classic way.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:24.177
I have to ask you,

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:25.611
we're almost out of time.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.180
The debt ceiling,

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.115
you have voted in the past

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.249
to raise the debt ceiling.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:33.019
In fact, three times even since 2017

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.822
Why not do it now.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.055
Yeah.

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:36.689
And I think

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:37.356
if you don't

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:38.858
you have catastrophic you know

00:07:38.858 --> 00:07:40.059
so you go elsewhere.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:41.360
Well I talked to Kevin McCarthy,

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.361
the speaker yesterday.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.896
He made it very clear,

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.331
I'm ready to sit down

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.533
with President Biden today

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:50.503
to talk about a reasonable debt ceiling,

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.872
which would mean more meaningful

00:07:52.872 --> 00:07:54.407
spending cuts.

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:55.408
The fact is

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:56.943
we should be having these conversations

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.244
right now.

00:07:58.244 --> 00:07:59.145
We know that

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:00.413
Secretary Yellen is going to put

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:02.648
she can put this off until June

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.584
June's going to be the target month.

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:06.586
But the speaker of the House

00:08:06.586 --> 00:08:08.888
is willing to sit down today

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:09.655
with the president,

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:10.523
the United States

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:12.158
and try to work this out.

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:14.594
And I would encourage him to do that.

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:16.295
House Foreign Affairs Chairman

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:18.097
Michael McCaul, thank you so much.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:18.631
Appreciate it.

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:21.367
And congratulations on your chairmanship.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.668
I haven't seen you since. Thank you.

